speechtext:
I beg my hon. friend's
pardon. I have under my hand the recommendation of the committee on that particular point. I am reading from page 318 of the votes and proceedings. If my hon. friend will look at the bill as it came to the house yesterday and follow the wording, he will find that the recommendation of the committee is word for word in the bill as it was presented to the committee.
(>b) The medical classification of the injury or disease causing the disability or death in respect of which the application has been made;
(ii)	The medical classification of such injuries or diseases as have been dealt with by the commission in connection with the application;
(iii)	Whether the injury or disease resultant in disability or death was or was not attributable to or incurred during military service or whether it pre-existed enlistment and was oi was not aggravated during military service.
Those words exactly were incorporated in the bill brought down by the government and introduced by the minister. In addition to that my hon. friend suggested yesterday that the grounds for refusal or acceptance of the pension should also be stated, and that recommendation was accepted by the minister.
